+
+# can be set to repair to maintain the integrity of the violation store
+# default is ignore
+freeze.store.default.integrity=repair
 ----
 
 This can help in CI environments to prevent misconfiguration:
 For example, a CI build should probably never create a new the violation store, but operate on
 an existing one.
 
+With `freeze.store.default.integrity=repair` the violation store checks its index file `stored.rules` and its folder
+as they are on disk every time it is initialized.
+Entries of the index that do not point to a regular file directly within the store folder are discarded,
+without touching whatever they point to.
+Entries whose file has no violations (i.e. the file is empty or only contains line breaks) are discarded together with their file.
+Furthermore, once all violations of a rule are fixed, the rule is forgotten, i.e. its entry and file are removed,
+instead of keeping an empty file.
+Entries pointing to the same file (by file name or through symbolic or hard links), as well as files no entry points to,
+are never touched.
+
 As mentioned in <<Overriding configuration>>, these properties can be passed as system properties as needed.
